@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Getting_Started}{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</h1>



<p>
    Every component NuGet package references the BlazorRamp.Core package. This Core package contains the "Live Region Service" and "Announcement History" component, but you can of course use
    this NuGet package on its own if you are only interested in its contents.
</p>
<p>
    In addition to the service and component mentioned above, the Core project provides a common set of CSS custom properties that all future components will utilise for their styling
    see Theming <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Theming}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview}"))">@GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</a> for more details.
</p>

<ol>
    <li>
        <p>
            Add the chosen BlazorRamp NuGet package using NuGet Package Manager or the DotNet CLI, for example:
        </p>
        <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CoreSnippets.Add_Core_Package" AriaLabel="Add Nuget package code block" />
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Add the following Core stylesheet reference to the <span class="code-span">&lt;head&gt;</span> section of your applications
            <span class="code-span">index.html</span> or <span class="code-span">App.razor</span> file dependent on the project type:
        </p>
        <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CoreSnippets.Add_Core_Style_Sheet" AriaLabel="Add Core stylesheet code block" />
        <p>
            <strong>Note: </strong>Additional component specific stylesheets would then follow for each installed package.
        </p>
    </li>

    <li>
        <p>
            Add the following Blazor Ramp Core live region script after Blazors script, as follows:
        </p>
        <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CoreSnippets.Add_Core_Script" AriaLabel="Add script code block" />
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Register BlazorRamp services in the <span class="code-span">Program.cs</span> file (Both server and client if using Server and WebAssembly interactive rendermode)
        </p>
        <p>
            Add the following line to the service registration section if you are using the <span class="code-span">Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection</span> package:
        </p>
        <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CoreSnippets.Add_Live_Region_Service" AriaLabel="Register live region service code block" />
        <p>
            For other Dependency Injection providers, register the interface <span class="code-span">ILiveRegionService</span> and its implementation <span class="code-span">LiveRegionService</span>
            as you normally would.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Add the <span class="code-span">&lt;AnnouncementHistory /&gt;</span> component with your parameter values above the Router component contained in either the
            <span class="code-span">Routes.razor</span> file or <span class="code-span">App.razor</span> file depending on your project type:
        </p>
        <CodeBox CodeBlock="@AnnouncementHistorySnippets.Add_Announcement_History_Component" AriaLabel="Add announcement history component code block" />
    </li>
</ol>
<p>
    That's it you good to go. For usage of the services or components please see the relevant section for more details.
</p>
<p>
    For information about using the Live Region Service see: <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Services}/{GlobalValues.Serivce_Path_Part_Live_Region}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Usage}")">@GlobalValues.Service_Name_Live_Region - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</a>
    and for using the Announcement History component see:  <a class="link" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Announcement}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Usage}")">@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Announcement - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</a>
</p>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Getting_Started}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Getting_Started}{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Accessibility}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>
